    Block {
      BlockType		      SubSystem
      Name		      "Position_Loads_EP1"
      SID		      "80"
      Ports		      [1, 1]
      Position		      [785, 292, 925, 338]
      ZOrder		      12
      BackgroundColor	      "green"
      AncestorBlock	      "KINARM_EP_loads/Velocity_Loads_EP"
      LibraryVersion	      "*1.120"
      MinAlgLoopOccurrences   off
      PropExecContextOutsideSubsystem off
      RTWSystemCode	      "Auto"
      FunctionWithSeparateData off
      Opaque		      off
      RequestExecContextInheritance off
      MaskHideContents	      off
      Object {
	$PropName		"MaskObject"
	$ObjectID		19
	$ClassName		"Simulink.Mask"
	Type			"Velocity_Loads_EP"
	Description		"<html><body>\nThe Velocity_Loads_EP block creates velocity dependent loads on the KINARM End-Point robo"
	"t in a global cartesion coordinate frame, based on end-point (i.e. handle) velocity.\n\n<br><p>Hand force (N) is calc"
	"ulated as: \n<br><p>Fx = A*Vx + B*Vy\n<br>Fy = C*Vx + D*Vy\n<br><p>where Vx and Vy are the x and y-direction fingerti"
	"p velocities (m/s).\n\n<br><p>Parameters A,B,C,D in the above equations come from the Load Table, with the row determ"
	"ined by the \"row\" input to this block and the columns specified in the \"Load Table columns\" defined below. \n\n<b"
	"r><p>The load can be scaled by a constant internal value or a Task Program-determined external value.  (Scaling of 1 "
	"= 100%)\n\n<br><p>Suppress positive feedback will ensure that A&lt;=0 and D&lt;=0 at run-time to avoid an unstable co"
	"ndition.\n\n<br><p><b>Warning</b> - Curl fields (valA=0, valB~=0, valC~=0, valD=0) should only be created with extrem"
	"e care as they can lead to highly unstable situations.\n</body></html>"
	Help			"Used to create a force vector for applying a velocity-dependent force field at the hand (fingertip).\n\n<H2>L"
	"ibrary </H2>\nKINARM EP loads\n\n<H2>Description </H2>\nThe Velocity_Loads_EP block creates velocity dependent loads "
	"on the KINARM End-Point robot in a global cartesion coordinate frame, based on end-point (i.e. handle) velocity.\n <P"
	">\nThe force output of this block is filtered using a 50Hz 2nd-order Butterworth filter for stability.\n<P>\nThe forc"
	"e field at the fingertip (N) is calculated as: <BR>\nFx = A*Vx + B*Vy <BR>\nFy = C*Vx + D*Vy <BR>\nwhere Vx and Vy ar"
	"e the x and y-direction fingertip velocities (m/s).\n<P>\nFor example, a viscous-based force field would be A=-0.5, B"
	"=0, C=0 D=-0.5.  The values of A, B, C and D are normally limited to between -20 and 20.  However, if secondary encod"
	"ers are used, the values are limited to between -40 and 40.  Units of A, B, C and D are N/(m/s).\n<br>For example, if"
	" the \"row\" input = 2, and \"Load Table columns\" are specifed as [1 2 3 4], then using the sample Load Table below,"
	" A = 1, B = 0.544, C = 2 and D = -1.\n<br>\n<tt>\n__________________________________________<br>\n|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"
	"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|Force A|Force B|Force C|Force D|<br>\n------------------------------------------<br>\n"
	"| Load 1 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0 |&nbsp;&n"
	"bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0 |<br>\n| Load 2 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1 | 0.544 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2 |&n"
	"bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-1 |<br>\n| Load 3 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-2 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&n"
	"bsp;&nbsp;-2 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;0 |<br>\n------------------------------------------<br>\n</tt>\n<P>\n<B>r"
	"ow: </B> this scalar input indicates which row in the Load Table the coefficients [A, B, C, D] will come from.\n<P>\n"
	"<B>Scaling: </B> this scalar input is only present if 'port' source for scaling has been chosen in the dialog box (se"
	"e below).  When it is present, the actual value of the loads output from this block are scaled by this input.  For 10"
	"0% of desired load, scaling=1. \n<P>\n<B>Forces: </B> this vector output is in global, cartesian coordinate space.  I"
	"t must be wired to the KINARM_EP_Apply_Loads block to actually apply the loads to the KINARM End-Point.  This output "
	"may be added to other Force outputs from other KINARM End-Point load blocks to create a composite load.\n<P>\n\n\n\n<"
	"H2>Parameters and Dialog Box</H2>\n<P>\n<B>Load on Dominant Arm:</B> indicates whether or not this load is applied to"
	" the dominant arm (checked box) or non-dominant arm (unchecked box). .\n<P>\n<B>Load Table Columns: </B> needs to be "
	"a 4x1 vector with the vector elements corresponding to the columns in the Load Table for parameters A, B, C and D.  I"
	"f a parameter is not going to be in the Load Table, then the value 0 should be used in the \"Load Table Columns\" vec"
	"tor  (e.g. if only viscous loads are specified in the Load Table, and the viscous parameter are in columns 2 and 3, t"
	"hen the \"Load Table Columns\" vector should be [2 0 0 3], which indicates that B and C are not specified in the Load"
	" Table and so both B and C are set =0).\n<P>\n<B>Source for scaling: </B> refers to the source for scaling of the loa"
	"d.  If the source is dialog, then a Scaling option appears in the Dialog box.  If the source is port, then a new inpu"
	"t appears to this Simulink block.  For loads that are always on, use a dialog scale with the value set to 1.  For loa"
	"ds that need to be controlled by the Task Program machine (e.g. to turn them on or off) or by an external block (e.g."
	" to ramp up a load), use a port source for the scaling.  \n<P>\n<B>Scaling: </B>  this dialog input is only present i"
	"f 'dialog' source for scaling has been chosen in the dialog box.  When it is present, the actual value of the loads o"
	"utput from this block are scaled by this input.  For 100% of desired load, scaling=1.   \n<P>\n<B>Suppress Positive F"
	"eedback: </B> if checked will suppress potentially unstable loads at runtime.  These include forcing A&lt;=0 and D&lt"
	";=0 (i.e. only allow resistive viscosity coefficients).  \n<P>\n\n<H2>Related Blocks </H2>\nKINARM_EP_Apply_Loads<BR>"
	"\nVelocity_loads_EP_(inter-arm)<BR>\n"
	Initialization		"library = 'KINARM_EP_loads';\nnumCol = 10;\n[inputname1, inputname2, inputname3, outputname, columnt"
	"ext] = loadBlockInitCommands(gcb, library, numCol);"
	SelfModifiable		"on"
	Display			"disp(columntext); port_label('output',1,outputname); port_label('input',1, inputname1);"
	Array {
	  Type			  "Simulink.MaskParameter"
	  Dimension		  5
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    20
	    Type		    "checkbox"
	    Name		    "use_dom_hand"
	    Prompt		    "Load on dominant arm"
	    Value		    "on"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    21
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "loadcol"
	    Prompt		    "Load Table columns [colA colB colC colD]"
	    Value		    "[A_VISC B_VISC C_VISC D_VISC X_SPRING Y_SPRING A_LINT B_LINT C_LINT D_LINT]"
	    Callback		    "%%%%\n% Because of bugs iN R2007, R2010a and R2013a (which have been reported to Mathworks), the f"
	    "ollowing code \n% is required here because in the Initialization Section it will ONLY correctly update those Mask"
	    " Parameters that are hidden\n% when the OK button is clicked (NOTE: the initialization code will correctly update"
	    " all Mask Parameters when the Apply button \n% is clicked, the bug is that it should also update everything when "
	    "the OK button is clicked in the absence of an Apply click)\n%\n% Adding a set_param call which updates one of the"
	    " mask parameters will call the initialization code to run, which \"avoids\"\n% this bug. This code should be remo"
	    "ved once Mathworks has fixed this bug.\n\ntemp = get_param(gcb, 'loadcol');\nset_param(gcb, 'loadcol', temp);\n"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    22
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      2
	      Cell		      "dialog"
	      Cell		      "port"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "source"
	    Prompt		    "Source for scaling"
	    Value		    "dialog"
	    Callback		    "sourceStr=get_param(gcb,'source');\nvis=get_param(gcb,'MaskVisibilities');\n\nif strmatch(sourceSt"
	    "r, 'dialog')\n	vis{4}='on';\nelse\n	vis{4}='off';\nend\n\nset_param(gcb,'MaskVisibilities',vis);\n"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    23
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "scaling"
	    Prompt		    "Scaling"
	    Value		    "1"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    24
	    Type		    "checkbox"
	    Name		    "stability"
	    Prompt		    "Suppress positive feedback"
	    Value		    "on"
	  }
	  PropName		  "Parameters"
	}
      }
